{
  "title": "Browser & application caches",
  "_comment": "Application-level caches. The Electron/Chromium entry uses * globs to match the Cache/GPUCache/etc. folders that Electron apps (VS Code, Claude, Slack, Discord, ...) create under Application Support. These hold only re-fetchable data. Chromium *browsers* keep their per-profile caches one level deeper (Google/Chrome/<profile>/...), so they need their own entry — the depth-2 glob above does not reach them. method: emptytrash empties ~/.Trash (irreversible). Note: only 'Service Worker/CacheStorage' is listed, never 'Service Worker/ScriptCache' — the latter holds MV3 extension bytecode and removing it breaks extension service workers mid-session. 'procs' lists the macOS process names of the apps that rewrite a category's caches while running; cdm warns before deleting under a running app. Names must match `pgrep -x` exactly (the CFBundleExecutable, e.g. 'Code' for VS Code) — an unknown name simply never matches, so a wrong entry costs a missing warning, never a false one. A 'kind: older-versions' row takes its globs from 'candidates' and keeps the newest match of each glob (see dev-caches.json and docs/DESIGN.md#older-versions). A path may start with @cache/, @temp/ or @boot-temp/ — this user's own C, T and X under /private/var/folders (DARWIN_USER_CACHE_DIR, DARWIN_USER_TEMP_DIR, and the folder macOS empties at boot); a cdm too old to know them matches nothing. 'kind: code-sign-clones' offers the app-bundle copies a Chromium browser makes at launch and leaves when killed, never one a running browser may use, sized by what they alone hold (docs/DESIGN.md#code-sign-clones).",
  "categories": [
    {
      "icon": "⚡",
      "name": "Electron / Chromium app caches",
      "method": "rm",
      "default": true,
      "desc": "Disk/GPU/code caches inside Electron apps (VS Code, Claude, Slack, ...), their per-webview partitions (e.g. one per Claude Code preview) and the agent SDK VS Code downloads — rebuilt or re-fetched when next needed. Cookies & local storage are kept.",
      "procs": [
        "Code", "Claude", "Slack", "Discord", "Notion",
        "Figma", "Obsidian", "Postman", "Spotify", "EasyEDA-Pro"
      ],
      "paths": [
        "~/Library/Application Support/*/Cache",
        "~/Library/Application Support/*/Code Cache",
        "~/Library/Application Support/*/GPUCache",
        "~/Library/Application Support/*/CachedData",
        "~/Library/Application Support/*/CachedExtensionVSIXs",
        "~/Library/Application Support/*/agent-host/sdk-cache",
        "~/Library/Application Support/*/CachedProfilesData",
        "~/Library/Application Support/*/DawnCache",
        "~/Library/Application Support/*/DawnGraphiteCache",
        "~/Library/Application Support/*/DawnWebGPUCache",
        "~/Library/Application Support/*/GrShaderCache",
        "~/Library/Application Support/*/GraphiteDawnCache",
        "~/Library/Application Support/*/ShaderCache",
        "~/Library/Application Support/*/Service Worker/CacheStorage",
        "~/Library/Application Support/*/WebStorage/*/CacheStorage",
        "~/Library/Application Support/*/Crashpad/completed",
        "~/Library/Application Support/*/Shared Dictionary",
        "~/Library/Application Support/*/Partitions/*/Cache",
        "~/Library/Application Support/*/Partitions/*/Code Cache",
        "~/Library/Application Support/*/Partitions/*/GPUCache",
        "~/Library/Application Support/*/Partitions/*/DawnWebGPUCache",
        "~/Library/Application Support/*/Partitions/*/DawnGraphiteCache",
        "~/Library/Application Support/*/Partitions/*/Shared Dictionary",
        "~/Library/Application Support/*/Partitions/*/Service Worker/CacheStorage",
        "~/Library/Application Support/*/component_crx_cache",
        "~/Library/Application Support/*/extensions_crx_cache",
        "~/Library/Application Support/*/logs",
        "~/.config/EasyEDA-Pro/*/Cache",
        "~/.config/EasyEDA-Pro/*/Code Cache",
        "~/.config/EasyEDA-Pro/*/GPUCache",
        "~/.config/EasyEDA-Pro/*/Service Worker/CacheStorage"
      ]
    },
